From 3711c38c075043306ed7e066737f8d5ab47fa456 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: strandly-the-agent <strandly-the-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:05:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] fix(strands): re-export the OpenTelemetry crates of the
 telemetry API (api-4)

---
 .rust-port/staging/p10fixb/decisions.md    | 2 ++
 .rust-port/staging/p10fixb/dispositions.md | 1 +
 strands-rs/strands/src/telemetry/mod.rs    | 9 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/decisions.md b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/decisions.md
index 6e4230b1d..dbcf40292 100644
--- a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/decisions.md
+++ b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/decisions.md
@@ -7,3 +7,5 @@
 **P-723. `AgentBuilder::trace_attributes` and `baggage_attributes` take any iterator of pairs.** Both fields stay `indexmap::IndexMap` (insertion order is the export order), and the builder setters are `#[builder(default, with = FromIterator::from_iter)]`, so `.trace_attributes([("session.id".to_owned(), AttributeValue::from("abc"))])` compiles without an `indexmap` dependency and a map is still accepted. Callers that passed `[..].into()` or `.into_iter().collect()` pass the array. Files: `strands-rs/strands/src/agent/config.rs`. Review finding api-5.
 
 **P-724. `DEFAULT_SERVICE_NAME` is private.** TS keeps it a module-private `const` (`telemetry/utils.ts:5`); nothing outside `telemetry/config.rs` used the Rust constant, so it is a private `const` there and `telemetry` no longer re-exports it. This amends P-482. Review finding api-8.
+
+**P-725. `telemetry` re-exports the OpenTelemetry crates of its API.** Under `otel`: `pub use {opentelemetry, opentelemetry_sdk, tracing_opentelemetry, tracing_subscriber}`. `TracerConfig::provider`, the return types of `setup_tracer`, `setup_meter`, `get_tracer`, `get_meter` and `tracing_layer` and the `SpanProcessor` trait `BaggageSpanProcessor` implements come from these 0.x crates, so an application names them through `strands::telemetry::..` and always gets the versions `strands` resolved, as `mcp` and the provider modules do for theirs. Review finding api-4.
diff --git a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/dispositions.md b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/dispositions.md
index 182ac8249..b0df4108c 100644
--- a/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/dispositions.md
+++ b/.rust-port/staging/p10fixb/dispositions.md
@@ -11,3 +11,4 @@
 | api-10 | Fixed: `tracing-opentelemetry = { version = "0.34", default-features = false }`; `tracing-log` leaves `Cargo.lock`; `cargo check -p strands --all-features --tests` and the telemetry tests pass | this commit |
 | api-5 | Fixed: both setters are `#[builder(default, with = FromIterator::from_iter)]` (P-723); callers in `telemetry/tests.rs` and `tests/live_telemetry.rs` updated; test `tests/api_surface.rs::trace_and_baggage_attributes_take_plain_pairs` (does not compile without the fix) | this commit |
 | api-8 | Fixed: `DEFAULT_SERVICE_NAME` is a private `const` of `telemetry/config.rs` (its only user) and the `telemetry` re-export is gone (P-724); no behaviour change, so no new test | this commit |
+| api-4 | Fixed: `telemetry` re-exports `opentelemetry`, `opentelemetry_sdk`, `tracing_opentelemetry` and `tracing_subscriber` under `otel` (P-725); test `tests/api_surface.rs::otel::the_opentelemetry_crates_of_the_api_are_re_exported` (lands with the api-6 commit, which adds the `otel` test module) | this commit |
diff --git a/strands-rs/strands/src/telemetry/mod.rs b/strands-rs/strands/src/telemetry/mod.rs
index 7ace0d2d6..d936a31ed 100644
--- a/strands-rs/strands/src/telemetry/mod.rs
+++ b/strands-rs/strands/src/telemetry/mod.rs
@@ -17,6 +17,15 @@ pub use config::setup::{
     BaggageKeyPredicate, BaggageKeys, BaggageSpanProcessor, Exporters, MeterConfig, TracerConfig,
     get_meter, get_tracer, setup_meter, setup_tracer, tracing_layer,
 };
+#[cfg(feature = "otel")]
+pub use opentelemetry;
+#[cfg(feature = "otel")]
+pub use opentelemetry_sdk;
+#[cfg(feature = "otel")]
+pub use tracing_opentelemetry;
+#[cfg(feature = "otel")]
+pub use tracing_subscriber;
+
 pub use meter::{AgentLoopMetricsData, AgentMetrics, InvocationMetricsData, ToolMetricsData};
 pub use tracer::{AgentTrace, AttributeValue};
 
